  "facts": [
    "The Callahan Tunnel, opened in 1961, was built to complement the Sumner Tunnel, carrying all northbound traffic under Boston Harbor between the North End and East Boston.",
    "In 1983, one-way tolling began, the Callahan Tunnel’s toll plaza was removed, and the Sumner Tunnel’s toll doubled to 60 cents, streamlining Harbor traffic.",
    "A massive 2013 overhaul replaced the tunnel’s deck, curbs, and wall panels, costing $19.3 million and temporarily diverting Logan-bound cars into the Ted Williams Tunnel and Route 1A."
